    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Both forms place one action after another; てから stresses the order and たあとで presents the following step.",
     "texto": [
      "The earlier action takes the て form in てから and the past form in たあとで. There is no need to repeat past markers in the English translation.",
